<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Friday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p>B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p>C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p>E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p>F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p>G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p>H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>   Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*   *G*    *H*</p>
<p>  Sep 16  18,188 3,256 21,444 12,390 12,427 3,974   616 17,033</p>
<p>  Sep 17  18,063 3,622 21,685 12,258 12,298 3,925   616 16,872</p>
<p>  Sep 18  18,126 3,309 21,435 12,191 12,226 4,070   616 16,945</p>
<p>  Sep 19  18,154 3,288 21,442 12,153 12,188 4,137   616 16,973</p>
<p>  Sep 20  18,899 3,245 22,144 12,131 12,166 4,575   616 17,726</p>
<p>  Sep 23  18,764 3,132 21,896 12,081 12,090 4,533   591 17,592</p>
<p>  Sep 24  18,746 3,291 22,037 12,036 12,039 4,566   596 17,550</p>
<p>  Sep 25  18,682 3,303 21,985 12,084 12,087 4,118   601 17,470</p>
<p>*A  Of the $18.68 billion in international reserves, $2.66 billion (14.22 pct) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0652</p>
